From e16cda2f64c0aa86ccef62e1475a8f0cf10e7121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:17:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 92/99] dock: Adds Window Maker's drawers.

"Add a drawer" in the Dock's menu adds a drawer's tile after the clicked
launcher: An entry of the Dock's `Launchers` with `Drawer = Yes`, an
`Id`, and its own `Launchers`. `wlmdock` shows its tile, with the arrow.
The compositor shows its row of icons, sticking out of the Dock: Its
launchers (compositor tiles, with balloons, double-click launch, the
dots and the stipple of launching), then its dock-apps (placed as
"Drawer.<Id>" in Dockapps.plist).

As on Window Maker:

* A double-click (or a click, with SingleClickLaunch) on the drawer's
  tile opens or closes it. With "Autocollapse", it opens after 600 ms on
  its tile (ClipAutoexpandDelay), and closes 1 s after the pointer left
  (ClipAutocollapseDelay).
* Icons are dragged into the drawer (over its tile, which opens it), out
  of it, and within it. Launchers and dock-apps of the Dock, the Clip and
  the drawers are handled as columns.
* The drawer's tile stays on the Dock when dragged off, unless empty:
  Then it is removed, with the kaboom.
* The menu of a drawer's icons has "Drawer options" (Keep on Top and
  Autoraise follow the Dock, disabled; Collapsed; Autocollapse) and
  "Remove Icon". The drawer's tile has "Remove drawer" instead of "Kill",
  which asks first, unless empty. Its dock-apps go to the Clip.
* Without Autocollapse, the drawer stays open (or closed): `Collapsed`.

Context menus are kept off an open drawer, which is above the windows.

